  "body": "It seems as though the power level check doesn't restrict users from adding additional room aliases. Here's the room configuration used to test:\r\n\r\n`m.room.power_levels`:\r\n```\r\n{\r\n  \"events_default\": 0,\r\n  \"invite\": 0,\r\n  \"state_default\": 50,\r\n  \"redact\": 50,\r\n  \"ban\": 50,\r\n  \"users_default\": 0,\r\n  \"events\": {\r\n    \"m.room.avatar\": 50,\r\n    \"m.room.name\": 50,\r\n    \"m.room.canonical_alias\": 50,\r\n    \"m.room.history_visibility\": 100,\r\n    \"m.room.power_levels\": 100,\r\n    \"m.room.aliases\": 50\r\n  },\r\n  \"kick\": 50,\r\n  \"users\": {\r\n    \"@travis:t2l.io\": 100\r\n  }\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nRoom members:\r\n* `@travis:t2l.io` - Myself (PL100)\r\n* `@turt2live:matrix.org` - Myself (PL0 - Plain user)\r\n\r\nAfter publishing the `m.room.power_levels` event above, the matrix.org user can still add aliases to the room.",
